{"name":"Rawhide","hex":"#865e49","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rawhide","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Untanned hide.","A whip made from twisted untanned leather."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clear (a pump) of sediment by starting and stopping it repeatedly.","To beat with a rawhide whip."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rawhide"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rawhide (material)","blocks":[{"text":"Rawhide is a hide or animal skin that has not been exposed to tanning. It is similar to parchment, much lighter in color than leather made by traditional vegetable tanning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Rawhide_chair_weave_detail_in_the_Jacob_Hamblin_House.jpg/330px-Rawhide_chair_weave_detail_in_the_Jacob_Hamblin_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rawhide_(material)"},{"title":"Whip","blocks":[{"text":"A whip is a blunt weapon or implement used in a striking motion to create sound or pain. Whips can be used for flagellation against humans or animals to exert control or strength through pain compliance or fear of pain, or be used as an audible cue through the distinct whipcrack effect. Whips are commonly used on horses to give subtle cues as tapping. The portion of the whip used for striking is generally either a firm rod designed for direct contact, or a flexible line requiring a specialized swinging motion. The former is easier and more precise, the latter offers longer reach and greater force. Some varieties have an extended stock section in addition to the line."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Riding_crop.jpeg/330px-Riding_crop.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whip"},{"title":"Rawhide (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Rawhide is an American Western television series starring Eric Fleming and Clint Eastwood. The show aired for seven seasons on the CBS network on Friday nights from January 9, 1959, to September 3, 1965, before moving to its eighth and final season on Tuesday nights from September 14, 1965, until December 7, 1965, with a total of 217 black-and-white episodes. The series was produced and sometimes directed by Charles Marquis Warren, who also produced early episodes of Gunsmoke. The show is remembered by many for its theme song, \"Rawhide\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e4/Rawhide-show.jpg/330px-Rawhide-show.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rawhide_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Rawhide (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Rawhide\" is a Western song written by Ned Washington (lyrics) and composed by Dimitri Tiomkin in 1958. It was originally recorded by Frankie Laine. The song was used as the theme to Rawhide, a western television series that ran on CBS from 1959 to 1965. Members of the Western Writers of America chose it as one of the Top 100 Western songs of all time."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rawhide_(song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Rawhide_mallet_in_Tuntorp_3.jpg/500px-Rawhide_mallet_in_Tuntorp_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Rawhide_mallet_in_Tuntorp_3.jpg/1280px-Rawhide_mallet_in_Tuntorp_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Rawhide_mallet_in_Tuntorp_3.jpg/500px-Rawhide_mallet_in_Tuntorp_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rawhide mallet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARawhide_mallet_in_Tuntorp_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Maasai_sandals%2C_1951%2C_